- U | work out on paper exactly why the firm failed | v: self-direction | chance: 80
- B | look for a backer, and plan to open again when the time is right | v: achievement, power | chance: 60
- R | tear up the old plan, and do something wholly new | v: stimulation, self-direction | chance: 70
- G | lean on the family for a while, until the ground is firm again | v: security, tradition | chance: 75
works: Within the year the debts are smaller and {N} sleeps through the night again.
works: {N} can think of the old friend again without thinking of the shut door.
fails: The months stretch on, and the failure sits on {N} like a weight.
fails: Money stays tight, and there are rows about it at home.

== bold: the shutters down on the friend's firm / B
base: look for a backer, and plan to open again when the time is right
likelier_if: has [good credit] +5; has [selling] +10
- B | borrow against everything you have left, and open again, smaller and sharper | v: achievement, power | act: borrow against everything they have left, and open again, smaller and sharper | chance: 30 | requires: good credit | grants: premises of one's own | title_if_fails: bankruptcy or insolvency in their history
works: The bank lends, the lease is signed, and {N} has premises of {Ns} own with a smaller, sharper business inside.
works: The second shop is half the size of the first and twice as busy, and the premises are {Ns} for good.
fails: The loan cannot be paid, and by the end of the year {N} goes through a formal insolvency.
fails: The second try fails faster than the first, the lenders go to court, and {N} is declared insolvent.

# ================================================================ a landslide on election night

== bold: a landslide on election night / B
base: go to the winning party's open meeting the next morning, for the doors it will open
likelier_if: has [organising people] +10; mark 'made a friend' +5; has [party member] +5
- B | give the new representative every free hour, and become the one they rely on | v: power, achievement | act: give the new representative every free hour, and become the one they rely on | chance: 40 | grants: friend in power | drops_if_fails: kind:career
works: By the summer the new representative rings {N} first about everything in town, and owes {N} a great deal.
works: {N} makes the office run, and the representative becomes a friend in a high place.
fails: {N} gives the campaign every evening and weekend, the day job slips, and the boss lets {N} go.
fails: The representative forgets {N} the week the office is staffed, and by then {Ns} own job is gone.

== bold: a landslide on election night / W
base: accept the result, whichever way you voted, and say so in public
likelier_if: years [good name in town] 5 +10; has [public speaking] +5
- W | stand for the council at the next count, to hold the winners to their word | v: universalism, conformity | chance: 30 | requires: good name in town | title: local councillor | takes_if_fails: good name in town
works: {N} knocks on every door in the ward, and wins the seat on the council by a few hundred votes.
works: The town trusts {N} to keep the new lot honest, and sends {N} to the council chamber.
fails: The campaign turns ugly, old stories come out, and {Ns} good name does not survive the count.
fails: {N} loses badly, and the things said on the doorsteps follow {N} round the town for years.

