# ================================================================ asked to stand for a child at the naming

== bold: asked to stand for a child at the naming / G
base: ask for the old family shawl, and hold the baby in it at the rite
likelier_if: has [old family name] +10; has [calming people down] +5
- G | gather every branch of the family at the old house, and stand for her there | v: tradition, benevolence | chance: 45 | grants: godchild | takes_if_fails: family who will always take you in
works: Every branch comes, even {parent}, and {N} stands for the child in the old shawl with the whole family looking on.
works: From that day the child is {Ns} godchild, and the family counts on {N} to keep her close.
fails: The old house fills with old grudges, {parent} walks out, and the family closes its door to {N} over it.
fails: The day ends in a row that {N} is blamed for, and afterwards the family's door is no longer open to {N}.

== bold: asked to stand for a child at the naming / U
base: ask whoever leads the rite to explain each part before you agree
likelier_if: has [public speaking] +10; has [scripture] +5
- U | learn the old rite word by word, and ask to lead the naming yourself | v: self-direction, tradition | act: learn the old rite word by word, and ask to lead the naming themselves | chance: 35 | grants: leading a ceremony | drops_if_fails: kind:faith
works: {N} leads the naming without a slip, every old word in its place, and is asked to lead others after it.
works: The elders listen, nod, and from then on {N} is the one the family asks to lead its ceremonies.
fails: The elders call it a slight on the rite, and {N} is turned away from {Ns} place in the congregation.
fails: {N} stumbles over the old words in front of everyone, and leaves the faith's gatherings for good.

